title: Server warnings
pid: b7845acc-1b0f-4d9c-a129-279797d7fd40
body: |2-
    - Request: ((request . "server warnings"))
    - Response: LP =((response-type server-warnings) (warnings ("WARNING" ...)))=,
      or =(warnings ())= when there are none. The warnings are the ones
      the server raised as it started: one per top-level key of
      skgconfig.toml it does not know (see "skgconfig.toml", below); one
      per skgrepo holding an illegal edit to a foreign node — a section
      of a node in a skgrepo of another owner than its home's — naming
      the first such node (ID and title), how many more there are, the
      skgrepo and the home, and saying that an owned one is shown only
      under the node and a foreign one ignored (=docs/telescopes.org=,
      "Illegal edits"); one per violation of the fork rules that a
      foreign note takes part in, naming both notes and which is foreign
      (=docs/data-model_technical.org=, "Hard validation constraints");
      and one per pair of one foreign owner's
      skgrepos that some node spans and whose dependencies manifests
      disagree about their order, naming the node, the disagreeing
      manifests and which skgrepo this server folds first (see
      "OTHER_SKGREPO_DEPENDENCIES.toml", below); and one if the server
      cannot watch the skgrepo directories (see "Repo files reloaded",
      below), saying that files changed on disk then need a rebuild.
      A reload of the config ("Rebuild session-lifetime stores") does
      not change them.
    - Each client sends this once per connection, as soon as the
      connection is up and before it requests any view
      ('skg-tcp-connect-to-rust', 'client.connect'). A non-empty answer
      is appended to a buffer, keeping what it holds, under a level-1
      headline "Startup warnings", each warning a level-2 headline:
      =*SKG Server Warnings*= in Emacs, =skg://messages/server-warnings=
      in Neovim. An empty answer opens nothing.
